@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Change your order's shipping address - Lively Help Center";
    ViewData["CategorySlug"] = "Buying";
    ViewData["SubCategorySlug"] = "Shipping";
    ViewData["HeroTitle"] = "Change your order's shipping address";
    ViewData["HeroStyle"] = "background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,0.4), rgba(0,0,0,0.4)), url('/help_centre_img/help_area/help_centre_hero_bg.png');";
    ViewData["IsArticle"] = true;
}

<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">

        <p>If your order is headed to the wrong address, don't worry — you may be able to update it, or get help from Lively Support or the carrier.</p>

        <p>Sellers aren't able to change shipping addresses after a purchase, but there are a few ways you can fix the issue yourself or with support.</p>

        <p><strong>In this article:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#update-address">Update your order's shipping address (if eligible)</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cant-update">If you can't update your address in Lively</a></li>
            <li><a href="#prevent-future">Prevent future address issues</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Not sure where your order is headed?</strong> <a href="#">Check your receipt</a> to confirm the shipping address.</p>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="update-address">Update your order's shipping address (if eligible)</h2>

        <p>You can only update your order's address in Lively if:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The seller hasn't created a shipping label yet (order status is still <strong>Preparing Package</strong>)</li>
            <li>The order is eligible for updates</li>
        </ul>

        <p>When you update your order's address, Lively will automatically use the new one once the seller creates the shipping label.</p>

        <p>If your order is bundled, everything in that bundle will ship to the new address too.</p>

        <div class="article-accordion-yellow">
            <div class="article-accordion-yellow__item">
                <button class="article-accordion-yellow__trigger" type="button">
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__icon">−</span>
                    <span class="article-accordion-yellow__title">Change your order's address on app</span>
                </button>
                <div class="article-accordion-yellow__content">
                    <ol>
                        <li>Tap <strong>Activity.</strong></li>
                        <li>From the <strong>Purchases</strong> tab, tap your order to open it.</li>
                        <li>Under the order's status, tap <strong>Shipping</strong> to (only appears if the address is eligible for changes).</li>
                        <li>Select a saved address or add a new one.</li>
                        <li>Tap <strong>Update</strong></li>
                    </ol>

                </div>
                    <div class="my-4 double-screenshot">
                        <img src="/help_centre_img/help_area/order_shipping_address_update.png"
                             alt="Change order shipping address in the Lively app"
                             class="double-screenshot" />
                    </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <hr />

        <div>
                    <h2>If you can't update your address in Lively</h2>
                <div>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Order not shipped yet:</strong> <a href="#">Contact Support</a> right away and include your correct address. If possible, we'll help the seller update the label.</li>
                        <li><strong>Order already shipped:</strong> Contact the carrier to request a reroute to your new address.</li>
                        <li><strong>If rerouting is not possible:</strong> The package may be returned to the seller. <a href="#">Contact our Support team</a> so we can help coordinate reshipment.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="article-info-box">
                        <strong>Tip:</strong> It can help to direct message (DM) the seller too, so they know there's an issue. They can't change the shipment address for you, but staying in touch keeps everyone informed while we work to resolve it.
                    </div>
                </div>
        </div>

        <hr />

        <h2 id="prevent-future">Prevent future address issues</h2>

        <p>Before you buy again, <a asp-action="ShippingAddress">check your default shipping address</a> so future orders go to the right place.</p>

        <div class="helpful-widget">
            <p>Was this article helpful?</p>
            <div class="helpful-buttons">
                <button type="button">Yes</button>
                <button type="button">No</button>
            </div>
            <span>80 out of 145 found this helpful</span>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>